<title>MALAYSIA: United Chemical shares suspended-KLSE.</title>
<headline>United Chemical shares suspended-KLSE.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of plastic products firm United Chemical Industries Bhd were suspended at the start of Wednesday afternoon's trading session pending a news announcement, an official at the Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The second board stock was last traded at 18.20 ringgit, up 30 cents on volume of 1.25 million.  </p>
<p>Company officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>In September, the company said it was acquiring a 100 percent interest in Hongkew Holdings (M) Sdn Bhd for 450 million ringgit.</p>
<p>The move will allow United Chemical to diversify into cement manufacturing and port operations in north-eastern Kelantan state.</p>
</text>
